<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idris II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/791">791</a>–828</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Idris II of Morocco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idris II was the posthumous son of Idris I, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. He took power around 803 and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> his capital, settling refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> in its two quarters. He granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> to his cousin, founding the Sulaymanid branch, and is venerated as the patron saint of Fez.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/idris-ii.jpg" alt="Idris II" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_of_Idris_II,_828_A.D.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Idris I left no male heir when an Abbasid agent poisoned him in 791, but his wife Lalla Kanza bore his only son shortly after his death; the boy, <b>Idris II</b>, was proclaimed imam by the Awraba at the age of eleven.</blockquote><a href="/empire/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 814 <b>Idris II</b> granted Tlemcen to Sulayman's son Muhammad, establishing a branch dynasty, the Sulaymanids, which ruled the city and surrounding region, formerly held by the Banu Ifran emirate.</blockquote><a href="/state/sulaymanid-emirate">Sulaymanid emirate</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volubilis">Volubilis</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. Died in Fez, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.04,-5.56&amp;year=815" aria-label="Volubilis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4408 930 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Idris II"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4858 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4858 1200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=34.04,-5.56&amp;year=815">What was here in 815 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
